msgid "narration/narrationText/ls_narration_1"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $highlightText}}TOP SECRET{{/}}{{titleParagraph}}{{@ class "
"$highlightText}}SECTOR: R-22{{/}} (Siegfried Perimeter){{pargraphStart}}The "
"sky over the sector is torn apart. The funnel is constantly bringing echo "
"tanks into our reality. The local garrison is holding the outer perimeter "
"but is pushed to their limits. If we don't change the situation, a "
"breakthrough is inevitable in {{@ class "
"$highlightSecondaryText}}[REDACTED]{{/}} hours.{{pargraphStart}}The ATLAS "
"complex has been deployed under the anomaly's center. This is our only hope "
"for it to collapse. While the echo cloaking is working, the enemy can't "
"notice the complex. But the anomaly...it's learning.{{pargraphStart}}We're "
"registering periodic bursts: This means an echo tank of an unknown type is "
"materializing. Its objective is ATLAS. When it reaches the point under the "
"funnel's center, it activates a gravitational pulse of such force that the "
"vehicles turn into scrap, and their crews turn into {{@ class "
"$highlightSecondaryText}}[REDACTED]{{/}}.{{pargraphStart}}We've already lost"
" three ATLAS complexes. Only a few more remain in our operational reserve. "
"If we lose these last devices, we won't be able to close the anomaly. The "
"breakthrough will be irreversible.{{pargraphStart}}SIGNATURE: CURATOR "
"(PROJECT M)"

msgid "narration/narrationText/ls_narration_2"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $highlightText}}ANALYTICAL MEMO 14/C{{/}}{{titleParagraph}}{{@ class $highlightText}}ANALYSIS OF FIELD ANOMALIES{{/}}{{pargraphStart}}To the tank group commanders.{{pargraphStart}}Captain Miller of the 6th Platoon was the first to notice the unusual properties of the Obelisks. When their shell accidentally impacted and cracked the crystal structure, the damaged armor of his tank...was restored. Unfortunately he didn't make it out of that battle. But his find will save hundreds of crews.{{pargraphStart}}Thanks to the ATLAS complex data, analysts deciphered the nature of the crystal structures. Remember this classification—this information will save you in battle more than once.{{pargraphStart}}We discovered three types:{{pargraphStart}}{{@ class $highlightText}}REGEN{{/}}\n"
" When destroyed, it emits a field with negative entropy. The blast wave of this kind of Obelisk literally \"bakes\" the micro cracks in the armor.{{pargraphStart}}{{@ class $highlightText}}BARRIER{{/}}\n"
" Destroying an Obelisk of this type releases a stabilization phase field that concentrates around your vehicles. This creates a temporary protective barrier.{{pargraphStart}}{{@ class $highlightText}}FAILURE{{/}}\n"
" When destroyed, a powerful phase pulse burst occurs. It disrupts the integrity of echo tanks' Mirium core and paralyzes them for a short time.{{pargraphStart}}Note: All Obelisks are in a firm phase bond with a certain group of echo tanks. Each hit at the crystal sends a destructive pulse over this bond and deals damage to the enemy units.{{pargraphStart}}Use the Obelisks in battle. This is the only way to fight the superior enemy forces.{{pargraphStart}}SIGNATURE: CURATOR (PROJECT M)"

msgid "narration/narrationText/ls_narration_3"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $highlightText}}TOP SECRET{{/}}{{titleParagraph}}{{@ class "
"$highlightText}}DIRECTIVE 22/A{{/}}{{pargraphStart}}We are one step from "
"victory... Or from ultimate defeat. In the last few days, we came closer to "
"the settings we need to forcibly collapse the anomaly. For the first time, "
"we have a chance not only to fend off the invasion, but to end it. The price"
" is high, though. Only several ATLAS complexes remain operational. If we "
"lose them, we can't replace them.{{pargraphStart}}REMEMBER: ATLAS is not "
"just a research station. It's your eyes. ATLAS predicts where the next "
"attack wave will come from. It analyzes the enemy's tactics and transfers "
"data to improve your tanks. Every punched tape delivered from the complex is"
" a step towards victory. Without it, we will be made blind and lose our "
"chance to stop the enemy.{{pargraphStart}}We can't lose more scientific "
"equipment. This is the matter of survival not only for the crews on the "
"front line, but for all of us.{{pargraphStart}}Protect ATLAS at any "
"cost.{{pargraphStart}}SIGNATURE: CURATOR (PROJECT M)"

msgid "narration/narrationText/ls_narration_4"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $highlightText}}FINAL REPORT{{/}}{{titleParagraph}}{{@ class "
"$highlightText}}STATUS: DECLASSIFIED (PARTLY){{/}}{{pargraphStart}}At 06:21,"
" the anomaly's activity completely stopped. The weather front is clear. All "
"Obelisk-type structures were destroyed. The threat is "
"averted.{{pargraphStart}}The collected specimens of the Mirium crystals, as "
"well as the remainders of the echo tank of unknown type were sent to a "
"special storage for further studies.{{pargraphStart}}Official statement: The"
" incident is over. The contingent's actions to hold the threat were "
"successful. The quarantine has been lifted from the "
"sector.{{pargraphStart}}{{pargraphStart}}{{@ class $highlightText}}PERSONAL "
"CURATOR'S NOTE{{/}} (Only for special reserves){{pargraphStart}}I'm "
"skeptical. We've won the battle, but not the war.The anomaly is just...gone?"
" We couldn't finish the calibration of the ATLAS complex in time. Analysts "
"are registering similar signatures in other regions but the number of bursts"
" is increasing. According to their data, we have three months before it "
"happens again somewhere else.{{pargraphStart}}My experience tells me that "
"what happened is just a light breeze before the storm. We need to prepare "
"for the next attack: update our weapons, prepare more ATLASES, use all "
"available resource—from Mirium technologies to simple and effective mine "
"fields. When they return, and they will return, we must face them fully "
"armed.{{pargraphStart}}The reports say the anomaly was learning to counter "
"our measures. So we have to be flexible. Yes, we study them and adapt as "
"much as we can—use their technologies and track their tactics. But how can "
"we be sure they're not doing the same?"

